@namespace NSail.Components

@* Detail on demand: what the element already says, said in full. It is never the only place
   a fact lives — a reader on a touch screen has no hover — so what rides here is the long
   form of something already on screen, never something only this can tell. *@
@* The declaration and nothing else: the bubble is one element in the browser's top layer,
   placed by ns.js after a steady dwell (ns-mud.css, THE WHISPER), so what rides here is the
   text and the box to measure it against. inline-block rather than display:contents — a box
   with no geometry of its own has no rectangle to hang the bubble under. *@
<span class="ns-whisper-host" data-ns-whisper="@Text">@ChildContent</span>

@code {

    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? Text { get; set; }
}
